import { FilesystemReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> FilesystemReaderCopy = FilesystemReaderCopy {
  summary: "Read and write files addressed by Path values, using a FileSystem service supplied at execution time.",
  taskTitle: "Write and read a small UTF-8 report",
  purpose: "Write café and Japanese text to report.txt, then read the same string back. This example uses a dedicated temporary directory, so it does not touch existing reports. The directory and its files are removed when the work finishes.",
  setup: "The imports name three modules effects, fs, and paths. effect fn report directory: paths.Path -> String defines work that receives directory and produces a String when executed. with FileSystem states the file service it needs; fails ReportError names its ordinary failure type. Within do, <- executes work and names its result on the left; _ <- waits for completion without keeping a result.",
  after: [
    "paths.child \"report.txt\" directory adds one filename to directory. It returns either Left carrying a problem or Right carrying a Path. |> passes the value on its left to the function on its right. effects.fromEither turns this result into work that succeeds or fails accordingly. Success gives us file.",
    "let text names an immutable content value. \\n inside the string is a newline. The arguments to fs.writeTextUtf8 fs.CreateNew text file are mode, content, and destination. CreateNew does not overwrite an existing file. The final fs.readTextUtf8 file returns the String that becomes report’s successful result.",
    "ReportError defines three failure shapes for this example: PathFailure contains a path problem, WriteFailure a write problem, and ReadFailure a read problem. effects.mapError wraps each failure in its corresponding shape. deriving Show allows show to produce display text for those values.",
    "main is the execution entry point. withTemporaryDirectory supplies directory, calls report, and cleans up afterward. effects.attempt turns an ordinary failure into Left or a successful report into Right. match chooses the message to display, and println prints the content followed by a final newline."
  ],
  details: [
    "Calling a function to construct an Effect, a value describing work, does not start a read or write. Execution from main follows the order in do. The execution environment supplies FileSystem. Importing a module or compiling for a browser does not itself provide access to OS files. Run this example as a CLI process.",
    "CreateNew creates a new file; Replace truncates existing contents or creates a file; Append adds to the end. Change text to edit the content, or \"report.txt\" in child to edit the filename. These operations hold the entire file in memory, so this is a small-file example.",
    "Pass a Path rather than a String as the destination. For text received externally, handle Left and Right from paths.parse first. Even a valid Path can encounter existence or permission problems, reported as FileSystemError. Content that cannot be decoded as UTF-8 uses a separate shape within FileTextError.",
    "Returning a Path from the temporary directory does not let you keep using its file after the work ends. Return the content you need, as this example does. Cleanup has been checked for success and ordinary failure here; those results do not establish guarantees for forced termination or cancellation."
  ],
  comparisonBefore: "TS can already express creation and readback concisely with Node file APIs, commonly calling a Promise-returning function and awaiting completion.",
  comparisonAfter: "Seseragi distinguishes Path, WriteMode, failure types, and the required FileSystem service. Constructing an Effect does not execute it, unlike an ordinary TS async operation that starts when called."
}
